**[Suggestion]** `findMetaTrigger` only fetches the preceding events page when the last page is partial (`lastPage.length < params.per_page`). When the last page is exactly full (100 events), only that page is searched — 100 events. When partial, both pages are merged — up to ~200 events. The coverage window toggles based on page alignment.

— Concrete cost: A popular PR with exactly 200 issue events where the `review_requested` event is on page 1. Page 2 has exactly 100 events (full). Only page 2 is searched. The trigger is not found and the review request is permanently lost.

```suggestion
    const preceding =
      lastPageNumber === 2
        ? (firstPage.data as GithubIssueEvent[])
        : ((
            await this.githubApi(
              () =>
                this.octokit.rest.issues.listEvents({
                  ...params,
                  page: lastPageNumber - 1,
                }),
              `listEvents(${ctx.threadId}, page=${lastPageNumber - 1})`,
            )
          ).data as GithubIssueEvent[]);
    events = [...preceding, ...lastPage];
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

`findMetaTrigger` 仅在最后一页不满时才拉取前一页。当最后一页恰好满 100 条事件时，只搜索该页（100 条）。不满时两页合并（约 200 条）。搜索窗口随页面对齐切换。

具体代价：一个繁忙的 PR 有 200 条事件，`review_requested` 在第 1 页。第 2 页恰好 100 条（满页）。只搜索第 2 页。触发找不到，review 请求永久丢失。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

