discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Critical]** `processMetaLane` dispatches the PR/issue body without checking `dispatchedBodies` first, so a re-fetched `review_requested` or `assign` notification for a previously-dispatched thread produces a duplicate envelope. — Failure scenario: Poll N dispatches the PR body and records `dispatchedBodies` for `owner/repo|pr:99`. New activity bumps the notification's `updated_at`. Poll N+1 re-fetches the notification. No `isDispatched` guard → fetches PR meta (extra API call), dispatches the same PR body as a second envelope. Contrast with `tryFirstContactBody` (line 511: `if (this.isDispatched(this.cursor.dispatchedBodies, bodyKey)) return;`) and `processPerCommentLane` (line 307: per-comment dedup) — both have the guard that `processMetaLane` is missing.

```suggestion
    } = ctx;
    const bodyKey = `${chatId}|${threadId}`;
    if (this.isDispatched(this.cursor.dispatchedBodies, bodyKey)) return;
    const meta =
      kind === 'pull'
        ? await this.fetchPrMeta(chatId, threadId, issueNumber)
        : await this.fetchIssueMeta(chatId, threadId, issueNumber);
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

`processMetaLane` 在下发 PR/issue body 前没有检查 `dispatchedBodies`，导致同一线程的通知被重新拉取时会产生重复 envelope。与 `tryFirstContactBody` 和 `processPerCommentLane` 不同，这两处都有去重守卫而 meta lane 没有。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

